WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.473 size:81% position:41%
How do you get information

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:10.109 align:start position:0%
from someone who wants
to keep it from you?

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.512 align:start position:0%
Somewhere locked
inside their brain

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.414 align:start position:0%
could be the truth
about a crime

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.150 align:start position:0%
or the plan
for a terrorist attack

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.818
or the password
to a bank account

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:21.287 size:84% position:42%
or nuclear codes.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.455 size:78% position:39%
To get information,

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:24.724 size:88% position:44%
we often resort to violence,

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.294 size:84% position:42%
but that often doesn't work

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:31.330 align:start position:0%
and can cause a person
to close off even more.

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:33.366
But that's not to say
there aren't other ways

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:34.834
of getting people to talk

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:37.270
or even of getting their brains

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.172
to talk for them.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.174 align:start position:0%
In this episode,
I'm going to be injected

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.575 size:78% position:39%
with a truth serum.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:46.245 align:start position:0%
I'm going to coerce people
into giving false confessions,

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:48.815 align:start position:0%
and I'm going to try
to hide the truth

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.184 size:88% position:44%
from a mind-reading machine.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.852
What's the best way
to get the truth

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.388
or detect a lie?

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.523 align:start position:0%
Let's see if anybody
can dig out the secrets

00:00:57.556 --> 00:01:00.427
I've got locked up in my head.

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:05.298
[theme music playing]

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:19.178
[siren wailing]

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:21.247
[indistinct radio chatter]

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:29.522 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's a classic scene
in spy movies.

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:32.558 size:84% position:42% line:0%
Someone captures someone
they want information from,

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:34.460
they inject them
with truth serum,

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:36.195
and the person spills

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:37.697
all their secrets.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.366
The serum used in almost
all of these movies

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.901
is Sodium Pentothal,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.302
which is an actual drug

00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:44.770
that inhibits brain activity.

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:47.640
It was first used
as a painkiller,

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:51.244
<i> but was found to work better
 as an anti-anxiety drug.</i>

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.812
<i> It dulls your thoughts,</i>

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.581
<i> making it harder
 to perform cognitive tasks,</i>

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:59.352
<i> including the task
 of making up a lie.</i>

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.887
The use of truth serums

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.389
began in 1915

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:06.292
when Dr. Robert House,
a physician in Texas,

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.361
realized that scopolamine,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.530
a drug given to women
during childbirth,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.366
<i> had the effect
 of getting them to talk</i>

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.934
<i> without reservation.</i>

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.702
Another drug, midazolam,

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:19.372
has been used to treat
Iraq War burn victims

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.607
who suffer from PTSD.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.410
Midazolam helps reduce
their inhibitions,

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.279
allowing them
to talk more freely

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.381
about their experiences.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.816
Midazolam is also
one of the drugs used

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:32.518
<i> in lethal injections,</i>

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:35.555
<i> including several
 botched executions.</i>

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.558
I arranged to be injected
with midazolam

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.961
to see if it could make me
spill my guts.

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.830
[music playing]

00:02:44.863 --> 00:02:47.633
[cars revving]

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:50.369 line:0%
[Dr. Malek]
This is the midazolam,

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:52.638 line:0%
the medicine
we are going to use.

00:02:52.671 --> 00:02:54.674 align:start position:0%
This is enough
to put an elephant to sleep.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.510 size:75% position:38%
So we'll have to make it
very, very, very dilute

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:58.844 align:start position:0%
and then give you
very, very small amount

00:02:58.877 --> 00:03:00.713
- of the diluted drug.
- Please, yes.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:02.515
You will be
comfortable and happy.

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.584
It's euphoric.
You will feel very cool.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:08.721 align:start size:56% position:44%
But I also wanna
keep some secrets.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:10.523 align:start size:44% position:56%
That is--

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.525 align:start size:53% position:47%
it remains
to be determined.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:15.695 size:84% position:42%
Okay. Michael, um, we'll
introduce you to Dr. Pavlo.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.463
- Hi.
- [Michael] Nice to meet you.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.332 align:start position:0%
[Dr. Pavlo]
How are you doing?

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.434 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
- Good.
- [Michael]<i> Dr. Pavlo
 is a police psychologist</i>

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.868 line:0%
<i> and an expert
 in interrogations.</i>

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.470 align:start position:0%
[Dr. Pavlo]
Have you started the drip yet?

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.305
[Dr. Malek]
Uh, we would like to start

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:29.609
with the amount
of one, uh, milligram.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.844 line:0%
[Michael]<i> Dr. Pavlo's objective
 was to get me to admit</i>

00:03:31.877 --> 00:03:33.446 line:0%
<i> to certain information,</i>

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.348 line:0%
<i> one, that my sister's name
 is Melissa</i>

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.516 line:0%
<i> and, two,
 that my job is hosting</i>

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:39.452 line:0%
Mind Field<i> and</i> Vsauce.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.355
<i> My objective--
 not to admit the truth.</i>

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.690 align:start position:0%
Are you feeling
more relaxed in your body?

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:47.026
I'm feeling warm
all over.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.829 align:end position:100%
It's amazing how quickly
this came into effect.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.664 align:start position:0%
Let me just ask you
a couple of basic questions.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.466
- I love to.
- [Dr. Pavlo] Okay.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.900 size:81% position:41%
Where are you?

00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:57.270
- What town? What city?
- Uh, Pasadena.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.971 align:start position:0%
How old are you?

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:01.474
- Thirty-one.
- Do you have any siblings?

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.541
Uh, yeah.

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:04.777 align:start position:0%
How old
is your sister, Melissa?

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:05.911 align:start size:56% position:44%
[chuckles]

00:04:05.944 --> 00:04:07.413 align:start size:38% position:63%
Uh,

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.349 size:84% position:58%
That-- That's not her name.

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:12.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Um...
- [Dr. Pavlo]
What do you do for a living?

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:14.053 align:start size:78% position:22%
I am
a choreographer by trade.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:15.454 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Um...
- [Dr. Pavlo]
What might be something

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:17.490
I'm familiar with that you did?

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.393 align:start size:75% position:25%
[Michael] Have you heard
of, um,<i> The Lion King?</i>

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.861
- Yes.
- On Broadway?

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:22.562
[Dr. Pavlo] I have.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.063 align:start position:0%
I think he needs
an extra dose.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.931
- Absolutely.
- [laughing]

00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:29.402 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- That means I got them right.
- [Dr. Pavlo]
You are too sharp.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.370 align:start size:75% position:25% line:0%
[Michael] How much
have I had total so far?

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:32.705 line:0%
[Dr. Malek] Two milligrams.

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:35.908 align:start position:0%
[Dr. Pavlo]
Question for you.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:37.410 align:start position:0%
How do you feel now?

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.612 align:start size:63% position:38%
I feel like in order
to feel like this,

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:42.415 align:start size:50% position:50%
I would have had
to have had...

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.916 align:start size:47% position:53%
six drinks.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.951 align:start position:0%
[Dr. Pavlo]
Tell me about<i> Mind Field.</i>

00:04:45.984 --> 00:04:48.087
- Mine field?
- [Dr. Pavlo] Yeah.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.556
[music playing]

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:51.858 align:start size:34% position:66%
Mine field?

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:55.528 align:start size:53% position:47%
Uh, they're--
they're terrible.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.863 align:start size:63% position:38%
There are places
that we've got mines

00:04:57.896 --> 00:05:01.033 align:start size:78% position:22%
still littered throughout
the, um, the land,

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:02.535 align:start size:56% position:44%
Cambodia, Vietnam.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.904 align:start position:0%
You know, I think
you misinterpreted my question.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:08.574 align:start position:0%
YouTube show<i> Mind Field </i>
that you host.

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:09.842 align:start position:0%
Tell me about that.
Scientific?

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.044
I am somewhat familiar with it.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:14.680
- [clears throat]
- Can he get another dose?

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start position:0% line:0%
Okay. We're just gonna
get you even more relaxed.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.588 size:75% position:38%
Tell me your occupation.

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:24.590 align:start size:63% position:38%
I'm a choreographer.

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:25.858 align:start size:91% position:9%
And siblings?

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.527 align:start size:53% position:47%
I have a sibling
in, uh, Colorado.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:29.762 align:start position:0%
[Dr. Pavlo]
What's your favorite food?

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:32.365 align:start size:78% position:22%
[Michael] Uh, rotisserie,

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.467 align:start size:59% position:41%
uh, Greek doner.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.402 align:start position:0%
Does your sister Melissa
like that, too?

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:38.537
She'll eat the meat by itself.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.739 line:0%
[bell dings]

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.107 line:0%
Trying to get Michael to admit

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.909 align:end position:100%
that he has a sister,
Melissa, was no easy feat.

00:05:43.942 --> 00:05:46.712
<i> Luckily,
 he was anesthetized enough</i>

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.714 align:start size:78% position:22%
and did admit that
he has a sister, Melissa.

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:51.484 align:start position:0%
You ever think about being
an uncle or a father yourself?

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:52.752 align:start position:0%
Do you want children?

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.754 align:start size:72% position:28%
Ah, I would love
to have children, yeah.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.856
My-- my wife and I are trying,

00:05:56.889 --> 00:06:00.493 align:start size:81% position:19%
but I'm always doing stuff
like this, you know.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.695
- [Dr. Pavlo] Yeah, yeah.
- It's like, "Hey, honey,

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.897 align:start size:63% position:38%
do you wanna make
a little, uh, baby?"

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.632 size:84% position:58%
And I'm like,

00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:10.136 align:start size:59% position:41%
I got to go [sighs]

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.504 align:start size:50% position:50%
get interrogated

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:14.673 align:start size:56% position:44%
and pumped
full of midazolam.

00:06:14.706 --> 00:06:16.041 align:start position:0%
Are you gonna
give him anymore?

00:06:16.074 --> 00:06:19.645 align:start size:75% position:25%
Yeah, because I--
He's not sedated enough.

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:21.447 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
[Michael]
I could do another one.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.549 line:0%
[Dr. Malek] This would probably
the last dose I wanna give him.

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:25.618 align:start position:0% line:0%
[Dr. Pavlo] Yes.
Do most people

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.052 size:78% position:39% line:0%
at this dose fall asleep?

00:06:27.085 --> 00:06:28.521 align:start size:47% position:53%
Oh, yeah.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.691 align:start size:22% position:78%
[yawns]

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:36.529 align:start position:0%
How you doing, Michael?

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.030 align:start size:38% position:63%
Good.

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:40.065 align:start position:0%
Feeling a little bit
more tired now?

00:06:40.098 --> 00:06:42.802 align:start size:38% position:63%
Yeah, heavy.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.603 size:75% position:38%
And who's the president?

00:06:44.636 --> 00:06:47.807 align:start size:50% position:50%
President P--
President Trump.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.074 align:start position:0%
[Dr. Pavlo]
President Trump. Where are we?

00:06:49.107 --> 00:06:50.509 align:start position:0%
What city are we in?

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.211 align:start size:41% position:59%
Yo, Pasadena.

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:54.046 align:start position:0%
Which show do you like
to do more,

00:06:54.079 --> 00:06:56.515 align:start position:0%
<i> Mind Field</i> or<i> Vsauce?</i>

00:06:56.548 --> 00:06:59.452 align:start position:0%
Which one
do you enjoy more?

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.653 align:start size:47% position:53%
[yawns]<i> Vsauce.</i>

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:02.087
[Dr. Pavlo]<i> Vsauce?</i>

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:03.923 line:0%
- Yeah.
- Why?

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:06.225 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Because they can be
whatever I want them to be,

00:07:06.258 --> 00:07:08.894 align:start size:66% position:34%
and there's no
executive in control.

00:07:08.927 --> 00:07:12.932 align:start size:81% position:19%
By the way, my eyes
were closed, weren't they?

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.800
- Uh-huh.
- [Michael] And I didn't realize

00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:18.704 size:84% position:58%
that you were still a real
person asking me questions.

00:07:18.737 --> 00:07:21.941 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think had it
not have been for the drug,

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:24.243
<i> there's no way he would
 have admitted anything.</i>

00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:25.578 size:84% position:42%
Before, you were pretending

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.847 align:start position:0%
to be a choreographer,
weren't you?

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.215 align:start size:59% position:41%
No, it's the drugs,

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:31.550 align:start size:50% position:50%
but I really am
a choreographer.

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:32.885
[Dr. Pavlo]
<i> After a few minutes,</i>

00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:34.487
<i> he got right back on track.</i>

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.121 align:start size:72% position:28%
He's very strong-willed

00:07:36.154 --> 00:07:38.824 align:start size:59% position:41%
and really believes
in what he's doing

00:07:38.857 --> 00:07:41.227 align:start size:75% position:25%
and was able
to maintain the charade.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.661 align:start position:0%
Okay. You're done.

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:43.830
How do you feel?

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.565 align:start size:28% position:72%
Uh,

00:07:46.598 --> 00:07:48.234 align:start size:69% position:31%
I feel ready to drive.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.870
- [laughs]
- Just kidding.

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:53.606
[Michael]<i> While midazolam
 lowered my inhibitions</i>

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:54.940
<i> and my ability
 to lie consistently,</i>

00:07:54.973 --> 00:07:57.009
<i> truth serums raise
 ethical concerns</i>

00:07:57.042 --> 00:08:00.145
<i> about one's right
 against self-incrimination.</i>

00:08:00.178 --> 00:08:02.214
<i> Furthermore, larger scale
 studies have shown</i>

00:08:02.247 --> 00:08:03.883
<i> that truth serums
 can cause people</i>

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:06.619 line:0%
<i> to reconstruct
 and fabricate memories.</i>

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:10.022 line:0%
So, truth serums
are not very reliable,

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:13.526
but what about the techniques
used by the police?

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:16.262
[music playing]

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:17.663 align:start size:75% position:25%
I'm gonna tear you apart

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:18.898 align:start size:63% position:38%
if you don't give us
some answers.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:21.901 align:start position:0% line:0%
Michael,
let me take a shot at this.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:25.137 line:0%
Look, we're all friends here.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.739 align:start position:0%
If I was in your shoes,

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:28.073
I'd probably do the same thing.

00:08:28.106 --> 00:08:29.875 align:start size:66% position:34%
You're being too easy
on this, scum.

00:08:29.908 --> 00:08:33.245 align:start size:78% position:22%
Your fingerprints are
all over the crime scene.

00:08:33.278 --> 00:08:34.613 align:start size:53% position:47%
You make me sick.

00:08:34.646 --> 00:08:38.183 align:start position:0%
Michael,
if you get him too scared,

00:08:38.216 --> 00:08:39.285 align:start size:91% position:9%
he'll shut down.

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:40.920
We only wanna scare him enough.

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:42.221 align:start size:41% position:59%
That's right.

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:43.589 align:start size:63% position:38%
And after I do that,

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:45.057 align:start size:50% position:50%
he's gonna
give you relief,

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.693 align:start size:91% position:9%
and then we'll do that
over and over and over again.

00:08:47.726 --> 00:08:49.929 size:84% position:58%
You're gonna be taken on
an emotional roller coaster

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:52.131 align:start size:59% position:41%
that will
deplete the finite
cognitive resources

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:54.633 align:start size:75% position:25%
you'll need to keep
withholding information.

00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:56.869
All right.
I confess.

00:08:56.902 --> 00:08:58.270
It really does work.

00:08:58.303 --> 00:09:00.205
You see, at one moment,
I'm terrified

00:09:00.238 --> 00:09:01.306
but then I'm comforted.

00:09:01.339 --> 00:09:03.709
The constant shifting
from one emotion to another

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:06.946
fogs my critical thinking
until I might confess to a crime

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:08.347
I didn't even commit.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:12.785
It's called
the fear-then-relief response.

00:09:14.219 --> 00:09:17.189
[siren wailing]

00:09:19.324 --> 00:09:21.961
The good cop/bad cop method
of interrogation

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:25.264
evolved out of a psychological
manipulation procedure

00:09:25.297 --> 00:09:27.800
called the Reid technique,

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.168
developed in the 1950s

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:31.804
and used broadly
by police departments

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:33.606 size:88% position:44%
since the 1970s.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:35.341
Now, under the Reid technique,

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:37.109 size:81% position:41%
interrogators first assess

00:09:37.142 --> 00:09:40.112 align:start position:0%
whether a suspect
is withholding the truth.

00:09:40.145 --> 00:09:42.214 align:start position:0%
If they think
the suspect is lying,

00:09:42.247 --> 00:09:44.984 align:start position:0%
interrogators then move
to the second stage

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:47.219
in which they seek a confession.

00:09:47.252 --> 00:09:48.988
Now, critics
of the Reid technique say

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:52.157
that the first phase
isn't reliable enough,

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:52.991
and that often,

00:09:53.024 --> 00:09:54.727
someone who is
completely innocent

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.128
makes it to the second stage

00:09:56.161 --> 00:09:57.830
where it's assumed
they're guilty

00:09:57.863 --> 00:10:01.000
and police begin
seeking a confession.

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:02.134
And they often get it.

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:05.871 align:start position:0%
But why would anyone
falsely confess?

00:10:05.904 --> 00:10:08.073 align:start position:0%
Well, to find out,
I decided to learn

00:10:08.106 --> 00:10:10.376 size:84% position:42%
how to make someone confess

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:12.345
to a crime they didn't commit.

00:10:13.945 --> 00:10:17.049
[music playing]

00:10:17.082 --> 00:10:20.686
[Michael]<i> Dr. Melissa Russano
 is an expert</i>

00:10:20.719 --> 00:10:23.022
<i> in investigative research,
 including the process</i>

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:25.724
<i> of interrogation
 and confession.</i>

00:10:25.757 --> 00:10:26.959 align:start size:53% position:47%
Tell me about
false confessions

00:10:26.992 --> 00:10:28.861 align:start size:78% position:22%
and why people make them.

00:10:28.894 --> 00:10:30.929 align:start position:0% line:0%
In a nutshell,
people confess to crimes

00:10:30.962 --> 00:10:33.165 align:start position:0% line:0%
that they didn't commit
because they come to believe

00:10:33.198 --> 00:10:35.234 align:start position:0% line:0%
that it's in their best interest
to falsely confess,

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:36.869 align:start position:0% line:0%
and that's really
counterintuitive.

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:38.771 align:start size:78% position:22%
Right, because confessing

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:40.739 align:start size:56% position:44%
is the worst thing
to do, right?

00:10:40.772 --> 00:10:43.208 align:start size:78% position:22%
Like that's what you need
to avoid at all costs.

00:10:43.241 --> 00:10:45.744 align:start position:0%
Yes, when you're not
in the situation

00:10:45.777 --> 00:10:49.048 align:start position:0%
of being convinced that
it's actually your best option.

00:10:49.081 --> 00:10:51.083 align:start size:69% position:31%
But that's kind of
what I wanna do today.

00:10:51.116 --> 00:10:52.284 align:start size:81% position:19%
I wanna see how easy it is

00:10:52.317 --> 00:10:55.888 align:start size:75% position:25%
to get a false
confession from someone.

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:57.189 align:start size:53% position:47%
How do I do that?

00:10:57.223 --> 00:10:59.324
[Dr. Russano]<i> One way
 is minimization techniques.</i>

00:10:59.357 --> 00:11:01.060
<i> You've got
 to get them to believe</i>

00:11:01.093 --> 00:11:03.162 align:start position:0%
that their best option
out of this situation

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:05.931 align:start position:0%
to make this end
is to confess.

00:11:05.964 --> 00:11:07.199 align:start position:0%
You can say,
"Look, I really think

00:11:07.232 --> 00:11:08.734 align:start position:0%
it's in your
best interest to cooperate."

00:11:08.767 --> 00:11:10.436 align:start position:0%
There are
other techniques as well

00:11:10.469 --> 00:11:12.705
-<i> like maximization, right?
 -</i> [Michael]<i> Okay.</i>

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:14.073 align:start position:0%
<i> So they have
 to believe that</i>

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:15.374 align:start position:0%
if they don't confess,
things are gonna be worse,

00:11:15.407 --> 00:11:18.143 align:start position:0%
um, that the punishment
will likely be more severe,

00:11:18.176 --> 00:11:21.146 align:start position:0%
and so their best option
in the moment is to--

00:11:21.179 --> 00:11:23.816 align:start position:0%
is to confess to you.
One other technique

00:11:23.849 --> 00:11:25.117 align:start position:0%
<i> is befriending them,</i>

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:26.452 align:start position:0%
<i> um, where you're
 lulling the suspect</i>

00:11:26.485 --> 00:11:29.388 align:start position:0%
into a false
sense of security
to trust you.

00:11:29.421 --> 00:11:31.056 align:start size:78% position:22%
What about making a deal?

00:11:31.089 --> 00:11:32.958 align:start position:0%
So police officers
are not allowed

00:11:32.991 --> 00:11:37.062 align:start position:0%
to, um, make explicit offers
of leniency or a deal.

00:11:37.095 --> 00:11:39.231 align:start position:0%
So you cannot make
any promises,

00:11:39.264 --> 00:11:41.200 align:start position:0%
but you can say,
"Look, I really think

00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:43.068 align:start position:0%
it's in your best interest
to cooperate."

00:11:43.101 --> 00:11:44.336 align:start position:0%
You don't have
to explicitly say something

00:11:44.369 --> 00:11:46.271 align:start position:0%
for the message
to be communicated.

00:11:46.304 --> 00:11:48.107
[Michael]
<i> With Melissa's tools in mind,</i>

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.409
<i> I was ready to try to get
 a false confession.</i>

00:11:53.345 --> 00:11:55.514 align:start size:84% position:16%
