the biggest response.

00:25:56.687 --> 00:25:58.189 align:start position:0%
So off to jail.

00:25:58.222 --> 00:25:59.357
[music playing]

00:25:59.390 --> 00:26:02.327
[Michael]<i> The P300
 concealed information test</i>

00:26:02.360 --> 00:26:05.630
<i> correctly identified
 which one of us was a thief.</i>

00:26:05.663 --> 00:26:08.099
But in this next test,
I will be the only suspect,

00:26:08.132 --> 00:26:10.335
and they will know
that I've stolen something.

00:26:10.368 --> 00:26:13.671
But the question will be,
what did I steal?

00:26:13.704 --> 00:26:15.306
Inside this room
are seven boxes,

00:26:15.339 --> 00:26:18.076
<i> and inside those boxes
 are seven different items</i>

00:26:18.109 --> 00:26:21.613
<i> that I've never seen.
My task is to open only one box</i>

00:26:21.646 --> 00:26:22.981
<i> at random and steal that item.</i>

00:26:23.014 --> 00:26:25.116
All right.
We've got a...

00:26:25.149 --> 00:26:26.885 align:start position:0%
a camouflage hat.

00:26:28.152 --> 00:26:30.254
And that's not all.
During this next test,

00:26:30.287 --> 00:26:32.323
I will be implementing
countermeasures

00:26:32.356 --> 00:26:34.325
to try to outsmart the test.

00:26:34.358 --> 00:26:36.794
<i> I will think
 a very strong thought</i>

00:26:36.827 --> 00:26:39.364
<i> every time something comes up
 that's irrelevant.</i>

00:26:39.397 --> 00:26:42.734
<i> Will that enable me
 to create brain waves</i>

00:26:42.767 --> 00:26:45.103
<i> powerful and dramatic enough</i>

00:26:45.136 --> 00:26:47.205
to not be distinguishable
from my response

00:26:47.238 --> 00:26:50.274
to the actual item
I'm trying to conceal?

00:26:50.307 --> 00:26:52.710
- Anne.
- [Anne] Hello. Welcome back.

00:26:52.743 --> 00:26:55.146 size:78% position:39%
I, uh, committed a crime.

00:26:55.179 --> 00:26:57.015
[Michael]<i> Wish me luck,
 because this time,</i>

00:26:57.048 --> 00:27:00.351
<i> there will be punishments
 like in the real world</i>

00:27:00.384 --> 00:27:04.022
<i> where getting caught in a lie
 can have consequences.</i>

00:27:04.055 --> 00:27:06.924
<i> And my friend Adam Savage
 was happy to advise me</i>

00:27:06.957 --> 00:27:07.992
<i> on my punishment.</i>

00:27:08.025 --> 00:27:09.427 line:0%
- Adam.
- Michael.

00:27:09.460 --> 00:27:10.762 align:start position:0% line:0%
I am going to be taking

00:27:10.795 --> 00:27:13.765 size:81% position:41% line:0%
an EEG lie detection test.

00:27:13.798 --> 00:27:16.100 line:0%
- Okay.
- If I lose,

00:27:16.133 --> 00:27:17.835
- there need to be stakes.
- Yeah.

00:27:17.868 --> 00:27:19.103
- Okay?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:27:19.136 --> 00:27:21.339 align:start position:0%
Naturally, I thought
of Chinese water torture,

00:27:21.372 --> 00:27:23.808 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i> which as you know
 from personal experience,</i>

00:27:23.841 --> 00:27:25.176 line:0%
<i> is when someone is restrained</i>

00:27:25.209 --> 00:27:27.278 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i> while water is dripped
 on their forehead.</i>

00:27:27.311 --> 00:27:29.747 align:start position:0%
And then right after that,
I thought, I know just the guy

00:27:29.780 --> 00:27:31.349
- to talk to about this.
- Okay.

00:27:31.382 --> 00:27:33.317 align:start position:0%
Because I--
I want it to be

00:27:33.350 --> 00:27:36.287 align:start position:0%
actually something
that I'm fearing and dreading.

00:27:36.320 --> 00:27:39.190 align:start size:53% position:47%
So, yeah,
we did an episode

00:27:39.223 --> 00:27:41.292 align:start size:75% position:25%
on Chinese water torture
on<i> Mythbusters,</i>

00:27:41.325 --> 00:27:44.028 align:start size:72% position:28%
and the creepiest thing
that happened

00:27:44.061 --> 00:27:47.165 align:start size:78% position:22%
after we did this episode

00:27:47.198 --> 00:27:49.467 align:start size:72% position:28%
was that I got an email
from someone

00:27:49.500 --> 00:27:51.035 align:start size:78% position:22%
from a throwaway account.

00:27:51.068 --> 00:27:53.971 align:start size:81% position:19%
He said,
"We found that randomizing

00:27:54.004 --> 00:27:57.742 align:start size:81% position:19%
when the drops occurred
was incredibly effective."

00:27:57.775 --> 00:28:00.812 align:start size:81% position:19%
That anything that happens
on a regular periodicity

00:28:00.845 --> 00:28:02.213 align:start size:53% position:47%
can become a type
of meditation,

00:28:02.246 --> 00:28:04.082 align:start size:50% position:50%
and you can then
tune it out.

00:28:04.115 --> 00:28:07.351 size:84% position:58%
If you couldn't predict it,

00:28:07.384 --> 00:28:09.087 align:start size:53% position:47%
you're-- he said,

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:11.823 align:start size:84% position:16%
"We found, we were able
to induce a psychotic break

00:28:11.856 --> 00:28:13.257 align:start size:53% position:47%
within 20 hours."

00:28:13.290 --> 00:28:15.493 align:start position:0%
Sounds like
the stakes that I want.

00:28:15.526 --> 00:28:17.295
- All right.
- Thanks.

00:28:17.328 --> 00:28:19.097 align:start size:63% position:38%
You're welcome, sir.

00:28:19.130 --> 00:28:20.198
[Michael]
<i> So now, under the threat</i>

00:28:20.231 --> 00:28:22.033
<i> of Chinese water torture,</i>

00:28:22.066 --> 00:28:24.736
<i> I was extra motivated
 to beat the lie detector.</i>

00:28:24.769 --> 00:28:27.872
[music playing]

00:28:28.906 --> 00:28:30.007 align:start size:53% position:47%
[Anne] All right.

00:28:30.040 --> 00:28:31.209 align:start size:34% position:66%
That is it.

00:28:32.777 --> 00:28:34.779 align:start size:75% position:25%
I was trying
to think about all kinds

00:28:34.812 --> 00:28:35.880 align:start size:78% position:22%
of frightening scenarios,

00:28:35.913 --> 00:28:37.248 align:start size:75% position:25%
I was trying
to tense up to make sure

00:28:37.281 --> 00:28:39.484 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was really uncomfortable
the way I was sitting.

00:28:39.517 --> 00:28:41.486 align:start size:66% position:34%
Well, for most tests,
that would work.

00:28:41.519 --> 00:28:44.122 align:start position:0%
But we will take a look
at this data and see...

00:28:44.155 --> 00:28:45.790
- [Michael] Yes, we will.
- ...what it shows.

00:28:45.823 --> 00:28:47.759 align:start size:44% position:56%
[sighs]

00:28:47.792 --> 00:28:49.327 align:start size:53% position:47%
Wow. Okay.

00:28:49.360 --> 00:28:51.496 size:84% position:58%
I don't think they're going
to be able to figure out

00:28:51.529 --> 00:28:53.765 align:start size:56% position:44%
what item I stole.

00:28:53.798 --> 00:28:57.001
<i> I really kept my mind active.</i>

00:28:57.034 --> 00:28:58.536
<i> I was going crazy
 with countermeasures.</i>

00:28:58.569 --> 00:29:00.905
<i> I was sitting uncomfortably,
 I was thinking about</i>

00:29:00.938 --> 00:29:03.007
all kinds of really
crazy things.

00:29:03.040 --> 00:29:04.408
I was thinking about like,

00:29:04.441 --> 00:29:06.277
"What if I have
diarrhea right now?

00:29:06.310 --> 00:29:07.979
How would that feel?
How do I hold it back?

00:29:08.012 --> 00:29:09.313
And maybe I do have diarrhea."

00:29:09.346 --> 00:29:11.082
All these things
that were sort of physical

00:29:11.115 --> 00:29:13.050
in nature as well.
I thought a lot about death

00:29:13.083 --> 00:29:14.886
and dying
and being dismembered.

00:29:14.919 --> 00:29:16.888
<i> And if they can get it right,</i>

00:29:16.921 --> 00:29:19.557
I would probably blame
witchcraft as well as science.

00:29:19.590 --> 00:29:21.292
[Dr. Rosenfeld] Well, it's--
I would say that's it.

00:29:21.325 --> 00:29:22.894 align:start size:34% position:66%
Yeah, okay.

00:29:22.927 --> 00:29:25.163 size:84% position:42%
[Dr. Rosenfeld] We're ready
to give him our best guess.

00:29:25.196 --> 00:29:26.364 align:start position:0%
Hello.

00:29:26.397 --> 00:29:27.231
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:29:27.265 --> 00:29:29.267
- [Michael] Are you guys ready?
- Yup.

00:29:29.300 --> 00:29:31.903 align:start position:0%
Let me ask you this.
First of all,

00:29:31.936 --> 00:29:34.405 size:81% position:41%
how confident do you feel?

00:29:34.438 --> 00:29:35.439
Pretty confident.

00:29:35.472 --> 00:29:38.009 align:start position:0%
What did I take?

00:29:38.042 --> 00:29:39.076 align:start size:41% position:59%
The camo hat.

00:29:39.109 --> 00:29:40.545
- Camo hat.
- Camo hat?

00:29:40.578 --> 00:29:41.579 align:start size:16% position:84%
Yeah.

00:29:41.612 --> 00:29:44.949
[music playing]

00:29:47.351 --> 00:29:49.287 align:start position:0%
[Michael]
That's impressive.

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:52.089 align:start position:0%
Did you see any evidence
of countermeasures being used?

00:29:52.122 --> 00:29:54.125
Not something I would swear to.

00:29:54.158 --> 00:29:56.027 align:start position:0%
Even while
I was doing the test,

00:29:56.060 --> 00:29:57.562 size:78% position:39%
I thought, you know what?

00:29:57.595 --> 00:30:02.066 align:start position:0%
<i> I'm reacting too quickly
 to the actual item.</i>

00:30:02.099 --> 00:30:05.837 align:start position:0%
I should also treat it
as though it's irrelevant.

00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:07.104 align:start position:0%
I should treat them
all the same.

00:30:07.137 --> 00:30:09.173 align:start size:72% position:28%
[Dr. Rosenfeld]
If you are consistently

00:30:09.206 --> 00:30:12.076 align:start size:56% position:44%
reacting to all
of the irrelevance

00:30:12.109 --> 00:30:14.445 align:start size:75% position:25%
with their specific
countermeasure responses

00:30:14.478 --> 00:30:16.581 align:start size:47% position:53%
that you formed
in your mind,

00:30:16.614 --> 00:30:19.417 align:start size:59% position:41%
they should produce
bigger P300s also.

00:30:19.450 --> 00:30:22.954 align:start size:91% position:9%
But the biggest will still be
produced by the camo hat,

00:30:22.987 --> 00:30:24.989 align:start size:59% position:41%
even if you were
countering it also.

00:30:25.022 --> 00:30:29.493 align:start position:0%
That means
I now have to be punished.

00:30:29.526 --> 00:30:32.463
[music playing]

00:30:32.496 --> 00:30:34.298
Science is improving
in its ability

00:30:34.331 --> 00:30:36.300
to read people's minds.

00:30:36.333 --> 00:30:38.636
And that raises some
difficult ethical dilemmas.

00:30:38.669 --> 00:30:42.607
We would have nothing to fear
from perfect lie detectors

00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:46.210
if the people using them
had perfect morals.

00:30:46.243 --> 00:30:49.080
So, the prospect of a
scientifically rigorous method

00:30:49.113 --> 00:30:52.149
of extracting information,
while exciting,

00:30:52.182 --> 00:30:54.218
is also terrifying.

00:30:54.251 --> 00:30:56.487
As we continue to probe
interrogation methods

00:30:56.520 --> 00:30:59.023
scientifically,
we have to also continue

00:30:59.056 --> 00:31:01.592
to probe them ethically.

00:31:01.625 --> 00:31:05.263
You know, Chinese water torture
isn't even Chinese.

00:31:05.296 --> 00:31:07.965
Its earliest description
comes from Italy

00:31:07.998 --> 00:31:09.367
in the 15th century.

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:11.335
And the Chinese name
was added later

00:31:11.368 --> 00:31:14.038
to make it sound
more mysterious.

00:31:14.071 --> 00:31:16.641
Oh, man, these irregular drops

00:31:16.674 --> 00:31:19.210
are supposed to drive you
slowly insane.

00:31:19.243 --> 00:31:21.345
You know, I think
this is a lot less

00:31:21.378 --> 00:31:25.016
about getting information
and more about punishment.

00:31:25.049 --> 00:31:27.585
And as always,

00:31:27.618 --> 00:31:29.087
thanks for watching.

00:31:32.022 --> 00:31:34.659 line:0%
[theme music playing]

